  "notes": "PT candidate changed from Adriana Accorsi to Luis Cesar Bueno (June 2026). Governor rows use the scenario with Bueno; polls whose only scenarios had Accorsi were skipped (Quaest 24-28 Apr: Vilela 33, Perillo 21, Accorsi 10, Morais 9, BNI 27). RTBD 2026-03-17, Paraná 2026-04-03, Gerp 2026-04-10 and RTBD 2026-05-12 rows are from their Bueno scenarios (Bueno polled 2-5% there vs ~10% for Accorsi). Paraná Pesquisas 15-17 May 2026 dropped: its Bueno scenario as published sums to 106.5% (Bueno 10.5% looks like a typo) and its other scenario has Accorsi. RTBD 2026-07-08 uses scenario 1 (with Telêmaco Brandão/Novo, who later did not run); Quaest 2026-07-28 included Cíntia Dias (PSOL) for governor (counted in Outros; she later ran for Senate). Paraná 25-27 Sep: Gazeta only showed valid votes; total-vote numbers taken from CNN Brasil/Jornal Opção (sum 99.9). Goiás Pesquisas (local institute, 24-25 Sep) from transmissaopolitica.com.br. Quaest samples: 1,104 (Jul) and 804 (Aug, Sep) as reported. PCO candidate is listed by TSE as 'Danilo da Silva' but polls call him 'Danilo Pinheiro' (Evangelista da Silva). gov_t2: Vilela x Perillo and Vilela x Morais were polled equally often; Perillo chosen as he was 2nd in most 2026 polls, but in late-September polls Morais and Perillo are tied for 2nd. Quaest Apr 2t (46/37 + 27 BNI = 110) dropped as inconsistent. Senate: Paraná Pesquisas (May, Jul, Aug, Sep) publishes sum of both votes (>100%) and Gerp Apr publishes 1st/2nd vote separately, so they were excluded for convention consistency (Paraná 8-10 Sep sum-of-two: Gracinha 42.7, Gayer 27.6, Calil 22.0, Vanderlan 21.6, Mendanha 18.3). Senate polls from Mar-May (RTBD Mar/May, Quaest Apr) skipped: they featured Alexandre Baldy and Delegado Humberto Teófilo (not in final field) and lacked Mendanha. Quaest Jul had minor PSOL/PCdoB/PDT/PV names later not running (in Outros). No Jan-Feb 2026 polls found.",
